Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.25,0:00:03.27,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(1290,1)\fnArial\fs20\shad0\b1\pos(320.612,303.429)\c&H2B322F&\3c&HF4F2F6&}Girtonia   Dark Forest, Defensive Line
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.24,0:00:08.79,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,Saint Heal.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.70,0:00:14.87,Default,Soldier,0,0,0,,The pain's gone!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.36,0:00:18.53,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,Take care now.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.80,0:00:24.08,Default,Pierre,0,0,0,,Excellent work.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.52,0:00:27.35,Default,Pierre,0,0,0,,On top of maintaining our barrier,\N you heal our injured...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.35,0:00:30.22,Default,Pierre,0,0,0,,I'm sorry to keep asking so much of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.22,0:00:31.30,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,Not at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.59,0:00:35.59,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,You and your team do the lion's share\N of the monster slaying.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.70,0:00:40.22,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(460,1)\fnComic Sans MS\b1\fs48\shad0\bord3\clip(m 278 176 l 276 174 275 170 275 165 276 160 278 154 281 150 284 147 287 145 291 144 294 144 296 144 298 139 302 135 305 130 311 123 317 117 325 109 337 99 352 89 364 82 375 77 391 70 408 65 423 62 444 60 461 59 480 60 496 61 513 64 531 69 546 75 560 81 573 87 583 93 594 100 607 109 617 116 626 123 633 130 639 137 638 0 1 1 0 359 259 359 258 334 259 318 259 298 260 273 263 249)\frz13.43\move(322.827,170.825,204.29,61.779)\c&H383246&\3c&H6945D8&}Uggggh...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.96,0:00:40.22,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I got so sick of bailing \Nmy old guard out all the time...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.76,0:00:43.60,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,I actually appreciate having the flexibility.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.43,0:00:46.40,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}More than anything...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.87,0:00:52.80,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}Aunt Hilde's return to saintly \Nduties has been a lifesaver.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.40,0:00:57.14,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}If not for dividing the kingdom with her,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.14,0:01:00.16,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}both the land and I would \Nbe in tatters right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.77,0:01:02.17,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}But even then...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.17,0:01:04.54,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}We've only bought ourselves a few days.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.05,0:01:10.42,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}The barrier Philia erected shattered today.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.13,0:01:19.90,Main - Italics,Asmodeus,0,0,0,,My shadow...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.10,0:01:22.85,Main - Italics,Asmodeus,0,0,0,,Bring Saint Philia
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.41,0:01:25.26,Main - Italics,Asmodeus,0,0,0,,to me!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.27,0:01:49.87,Default,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(710,1)\blur4\t(1,710,\blur0)\an8\fnGeorgia\b1\fs18\shad0\bord0\c&HDA8FA9&}The Too-Perfect Saint: Tossed Aside\Nby My Fiancé and Sold to Another Kingdom
Dialogue: 1,0:01:47.89,0:01:49.87,Default,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(960,1)\an8\fnGeorgia\b1\fs18\shad0\bord0\c&H884FD9&\3c&HFCFEFE&}The Too-Perfect Saint{\c&H9B9999&}: {\c&HDEC58D&}Tossed {\c&HDDBF93&}Aside\N{\c&HE2B99A&}by {\c&HC8ACAD&}My {\c&HDDB3B4&}Fiancé {\c&HDCBAC3&}and {\c&HD79BB3&}Sold {\c&HCEA8CE&}to {\c&HD4A8D5&}Another {\c&HC3A8E2&}Kingdom
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.61,0:03:00.78,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(690,1)\shad1\bord0\fnGeorgia\fs10\c&HF9F8FA&\3c&H4E4E4E&\4c&H252526&\pos(492,283.044)}Episode 8\N"With {\fs12\c&H0CDD21&}You{\fs10\c&HF9F8FA&}, Who Gave Me {\fs12\c&H0CDD21&}Courage{\fs10\c&HF9F8FA&}"
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.32,0:03:04.58,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Saint Bind.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.73,0:03:13.29,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Who are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.80,0:03:18.05,Default,Erza,0,0,0,,First time seeing a demon?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.17,0:03:25.23,Default,Erza,0,0,0,,It's a pleasure to meet you, \NMiss Greatest of All Time.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.47,0:03:28.48,Default,Erza,0,0,0,,My name is Erza Notice.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.31,0:03:30.56,Default,Erza,0,0,0,,I'm an exorcist.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.29,0:03:32.78,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,An exorcist?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.78,0:03:36.07,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,The demon hunters from the Church of Cremoux?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.58,0:03:39.03,Default,Erza,0,0,0,,You're as smart as they say.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.03,0:03:43.41,Default,Erza,0,0,0,,I came to warn you about the \Napproach of the Demon Realm
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.41,0:03:45.45,Default,Erza,0,0,0,,that happens every few centuries.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.45,0:03:50.54,Default,Erza,0,0,0,,But I wasn't expecting {\i1}him{\i0} to have \Nstrengthened enough to send his shadow.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.62,0:03:54.28,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Do you mean the archdemon Asmodeus?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.00,0:03:58.09,Default,Erza,0,0,0,,Oh? You know about that, too?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.68,0:04:01.70,Default,Erza,0,0,0,,If the power of the Demon Realm \Ncontinues to wax,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.70,0:04:06.26,Default,Erza,0,0,0,,the sealed archdemon, Asmodeus, \Nwill revive for sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.26,0:04:09.75,Default,Erza,0,0,0,,And his first target...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.69,0:04:13.69,Default,Erza,0,0,0,,will be you, Saint Philia.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.32,0:04:19.43,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have an in-name-only national \Ndefense meeting coming up.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.01,0:04:24.14,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}Maybe I'll check on \NPrince Fernand beforehand.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.95,0:04:32.59,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I was so busy yesterday hunting \Nmonsters and reforming the barrier,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.59,0:04:35.22,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I didn't have time to try \Npersuading him again...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.22,0:04:36.42,Default,Pyrz,0,0,0,,Saint Mia?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.30,0:04:39.64,Default,Pyrz,0,0,0,,Where might you be off to?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.64,0:04:42.26,Default,Pyrz,0,0,0,,That's not the way to the conference room.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.26,0:04:43.67,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,Marquis Pyrz?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.15,0:04:46.41,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}A supporter of Prince Julius's.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.41,0:04:48.91,Main - Italics,Mia,0,0,0,,The strongest backer of the\Nsecond prince faction, even.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.91,0:04:54.35,Default,Pyrz,0,0,0,,I've heard word that you've been \Nfrequenting Prince Fernand's villa.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.35,0:04:57.81,Default,Pyrz,0,0,0,,What kind of behavior is that\N for an affianced girl?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.81,0:05:01.37,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,My fiancé's brother is in poor health.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.37,0:05:04.90,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,What kind of saint would I be \Nif I showed no concern for him?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.90,0:05:09.26,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,I also thought it might help\Nto improve my healing techniques,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.26,0:05:12.77,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,so I took it upon myself \Nto pay him a house call.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.79,0:05:18.32,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,But he turns me away\N every time, I'm afraid...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.53,0:05:20.88,Default,Pyrz,0,0,0,,Oh, is that all it is?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.88,0:05:23.38,Default,Pyrz,0,0,0,,What a beneficent saint we have.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.38,0:05:25.82,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}He's clearly relieved to hear that.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.82,0:05:29.26,Default,Pyrz,0,0,0,,However, it would be best \Nfor you to leave him be.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.58,0:05:32.81,Default,Pyrz,0,0,0,,It's his choice to be housebound, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.67,0:05:40.73,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's the way you've treated him\Nthat made him close his heart off so!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.39,0:05:43.90,Default,Pyrz's Son,0,0,0,,It's time.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.90,0:05:45.62,Default,Pyrz's Son,0,0,0,,Let's go to the conference room.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.40,0:05:46.86,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,Wh...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.19,0:05:47.82,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,Wh...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.22,0:05:49.20,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.68,0:05:53.52,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,What are {\i1}you{\i0} doing here, Fernand?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.52,0:05:55.70,Default,Fernand,0,0,0,,Watch your tongue, Julius.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.00,0:06:01.29,Default,Fernand,0,0,0,,You should show your \Nelder brother more respect.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.30,0:06:08.99,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}Why, after he was so determined \Nnot to leave his room...?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.83,0:06:15.27,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,I'm delighted to see you in good spirits.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.67,0:06:18.48,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,But shouldn't you be in bed right now?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.48,0:06:22.02,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,It's not good for your health\N to overexert yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.48,0:06:26.39,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}That's true. I hope he can take this.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.39,0:06:27.95,Default,Fernand,0,0,0,,I appreciate your concern.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.95,0:06:31.32,Default,Fernand,0,0,0,,But I'm feeling quite well at the moment.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.65,0:06:33.78,Default,Fernand,0,0,0,,With our father taken ill,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.78,0:06:36.11,Default,Fernand,0,0,0,,it's important that I step in...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.11,0:06:37.79,Default,Fernand,0,0,0,,as the crown prince.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.66,0:06:42.90,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}Prince Fernand! Isn't that too far a step?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.90,0:06:46.39,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}You don't know what he might \Ntry if you provoke him!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.39,0:06:47.46,Default,Fernand,0,0,0,,This is what I want.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.04,0:06:50.97,Default,Fernand,0,0,0,,To force my brother to make a move.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.22,0:06:57.56,Default,Fernand,0,0,0,,Really, I can't believe you unilaterally \Nrefused Parnacorta's aid.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.56,0:07:01.47,Default,Fernand,0,0,0,,Their king is an old friend of our father's.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.47,0:07:03.26,Default,Fernand,0,0,0,,Our kingdoms are allies, so—
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.26,0:07:04.36,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,Never mind that!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.36,0:07:08.28,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,It's obvious they have an ulterior motive\N in sending their knights here!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.28,0:07:11.84,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,They want to capitalize \Non the chaos and take us over!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.84,0:07:12.91,Default,Fernand,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.91,0:07:16.82,Default,Fernand,0,0,0,,A kingdom about to be ravaged by monsters?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.82,0:07:18.62,Default,Fernand,0,0,0,,That'd be a funny thing to take over.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.65,0:07:24.95,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I thought he'd be more \Nafraid of Prince Julius,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.95,0:07:26.65,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}but he's handling himself well.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.09,0:07:32.34,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}No... he's putting on a front.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.34,0:07:35.39,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}Of course he hasn't recovered this quickly.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.39,0:07:37.68,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}Trauma doesn't disappear overnight either.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.46,0:07:40.94,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}But he's still rising to the occasion.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.65,0:07:46.32,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}In that case, as the one who spurred him \Nto this, I need to support him!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.64,0:07:50.40,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I won't let the one fighting\N on the front line get hurt!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.20,0:07:55.17,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,Brother, that's a ridiculous argument.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.17,0:07:56.74,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,And then there's Philia!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.37,0:08:02.18,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,The fact that she refused my demand for \Nher return shows she's working for them now!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.18,0:08:05.75,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,What kind of unfeeling woman refuses\Nto aid her homeland in its hour of need?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.00,0:08:10.05,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,She's a traitor! \NWe should arrest her for treason!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.76,0:08:16.80,Default,Fernand,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh no! Mia's exceeded her anger \Nlimit and gone completely blank!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.35,0:08:20.00,Default,Fernand,0,0,0,,Goodness gracious.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.00,0:08:23.44,Default,Fernand,0,0,0,,It should have been obvious \NParnacorta would never accept.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.44,0:08:25.97,Default,Fernand,0,0,0,,Let's stop with these childish tantrums
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.97,0:08:28.01,Default,Fernand,0,0,0,,and discuss a few more constructive ideas—
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.01,0:08:29.69,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,You be quiet, Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.00,0:08:35.20,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,All right! Our first duty is to strip \NMarquess Adenauer of his assets and title!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.60,0:08:39.36,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,The parents of the traitor must be punished!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.36,0:08:41.65,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,This conference is hereby over!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.65,0:08:43.91,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,You're all dismissed!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.23,0:08:49.21,Default,Fernand,0,0,0,,I'm sorry. That's the best I could do for now.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.21,0:08:52.00,Default,Fernand,0,0,0,,The medicine's worn off.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.00,0:08:53.67,Default,Fernand,0,0,0,,Inconvenient, I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.67,0:08:56.66,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,Not at all. \NYou did wonderfully, Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.66,0:08:58.62,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,You deserve a nice, long rest.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.62,0:09:01.52,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,Thank you so much for being brave.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.91,0:09:04.40,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,You were really very dashing back there!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.62,0:09:10.32,Default,Fernand,0,0,0,,Was I? It was worth making the trip, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.82,0:09:13.09,Default,Fernand,0,0,0,,But Mia, please be careful.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.14,0:09:15.71,Default,Cornelia,0,0,0,,You're confiscating our assets?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.71,0:09:17.20,Default,George,0,0,0,,Y-You can't do that!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.20,0:09:19.10,Default,George,0,0,0,,You have no good reason—
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.10,0:09:20.87,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,If you wish to avoid it,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.16,0:09:25.95,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,then assist me with my plan!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.95,0:09:29.36,Default,Fernand,0,0,0,,My provocation will incite\N my brother to action.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.36,0:09:33.16,Default,Fernand,0,0,0,,We need to use this opportunity \Nto expose him for what he is.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.16,0:09:35.88,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,Yes, this is the critical moment.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.34,0:09:39.14,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,So let's make it official, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.55,0:09:41.68,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,Will you fight with me?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.57,0:09:48.69,Default,Fernand,0,0,0,,Of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.15,0:09:52.27,Default,Fernand,0,0,0,,With you, who gave me courage.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.38,0:10:06.83,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,You're...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.51,0:10:10.42,Default,Pierre,0,0,0,,Former Saint Hildegarde.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.19,0:10:13.05,Default,Pierre,0,0,0,,There's something I need to discuss with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.05,0:10:15.05,Default,Sign,0,0,0,,{\an2\fnGeorgia\b1\fs10\shad0\bord0\c&H884FD9&\pos(323,110)}The Too-Perfect Saint{\c&H9B9999&}: {\c&HDEC58D&}Tossed {\c&HDDBF93&}Aside\N{\c&HE2B99A&}by {\c&HC8ACAD&}My {\c&HDDB3B4&}Fiancé {\c&HDCBAC3&}and {\c&HD79BB3&}Sold {\c&HCEA8CE&}to {\c&HD4A8D5&}Another {\c&HC3A8E2&}Kingdom
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.05,0:10:17.55,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,1)\fnArial\fs18\b1\shad0\pos(320,296.082)\c&HF5FDFE&\3c&H3F4040&}Kingdom of Bolmern  Mattilas Estate
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.92,0:10:17.55,Main - Top,Emily,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.55,0:10:20.84,Default,Emily,0,0,0,,You want me to help expand the \NGreat Purification Circle?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.19,0:10:25.97,Default,Emily,0,0,0,,You expect me to play second \Nfiddle to the likes of Philia Adenauer?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.97,0:10:28.48,Default,Grace,0,0,0,,Yes, Big Sister Emily.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.19,0:10:30.90,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(310,1)\fnGeorgia\fs10\shad0\blur4\c&H3E2BC2&\3c&HEFF5F2&\b1\pos(488.534,256.939)}Eldest Daughter of the Mattilas Family\N {\fs14\c&H3D51CF&}Emily Mattilas
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.90,0:10:35.28,Default,Grace,0,0,0,,I've already discussed the plan with Father.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.28,0:10:38.65,Default,Grace,0,0,0,,He was overjoyed and ran right off\N to get the king's permission.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.44,0:10:36.86,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(110,520)\fnArial\b1\bord1\shad0\frz9.762\c&H3933D9&\3c&H00274B&\pos(370.22,38.817)}Sounds great!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.65,0:10:42.41,Default,Emily,0,0,0,,Now you've got Father playing messenger \Nboy for the kingdom next door?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.41,0:10:43.66,Default,Emily,0,0,0,,This is utter madness!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.98,0:10:45.41,Default,Emily,0,0,0,,Not to mention...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.41,0:10:49.20,Main - Top,Emily,0,0,0,,This is all for the likes of Philia Adenauer?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.92,0:10:50.92,Default,Grace,0,0,0,,{\i1}I had a feeling this would happen.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.27,0:10:57.59,Default,Grace,0,0,0,,{\i1}Big Sister Emily sees Philia,\Nthe greatest saint of all time, as her rival.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.59,0:11:02.92,Default,Emila,0,0,0,,Besides, our efforts alone have \Nbeen enough to keep Bolmern safe!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.92,0:11:06.03,Default,Emila,0,0,0,,As the eldest daughter \Nof the Mattilas family, I say we—
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.25,0:11:06.72,Main - Top,Amanda,0,0,0,,Okay, that's enough.
Dialogue: 1,0:11:07.10,0:11:08.71,Default,Amanda,0,0,0,,Big Sister Emily,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.77,0:11:14.90,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\an8\fad(310,1)\fnGeorgia\fs10\shad0\blur4\c&H3E2BC2&\3c&HEFF5F2&\b1\pos(168.84,76.327)}Third Daughter of the Mattilas Family\N {\fs14\c&H3D51CF&}Jane Mattilas
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.77,0:11:14.90,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(310,1)\fnGeorgia\fs10\shad0\blur4\c&H3E2BC2&\3c&HEFF5F2&\b1\pos(494.046,283.266)}Second Daughter of the Mattilas Family\N {\fs14\c&H3D51CF&}Amanda Mattilas
Dialogue: 1,0:11:08.71,0:11:12.22,Default,Amanda,0,0,0,,the monster threat will only worsen.
Dialogue: 1,0:11:12.22,0:11:14.90,Default,Amanda,0,0,0,,As bright as you are, I'm sure you know that.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.90,0:11:15.73,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(1,690)\bord3\shad1\an4\fnArial Black\fs48\c&H723657&\3c&HFBF4F4&}U{\fs36}RK
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.73,0:11:16.78,Default,Emily,0,0,0,,Well, I...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.59,0:11:21.44,Default,Jane,0,0,0,,I think Big Sister Emily is jealous of Philia!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.06,0:11:25.20,Default,Jane,0,0,0,,Though that would hardly\N be becoming of a saint.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.55,0:11:27.38,Default,Emily,0,0,0,,Jane, y-you be quiet!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.38,0:11:30.37,Default,Emily,0,0,0,,I am most certainly not \Ngiven to such petty feelings!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.87,0:11:33.02,Default,Emily,0,0,0,,I just have to do it, don't I?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.02,0:11:35.38,Default,Emily,0,0,0,,It's my duty as a saint, I suppose!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.38,0:11:38.44,Default,Grace,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'm glad it all worked out.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.40,0:11:38.44,Main - Top,Emily,0,0,0,,Don't get the wrong idea!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.44,0:11:41.93,Default,Emily,0,0,0,,I {\i1}barely{\i0} think about Philia Adenauer!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.93,0:11:44.26,Default,Grace,0,0,0,,{\i1}Thank you so much, Big Sister Jane!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.01,0:11:49.85,Default,Emily,0,0,0,,Now, what would you like us to do?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.85,0:11:51.96,Default,Grace,0,0,0,,To expand the Great Purification Circle,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.96,0:11:55.40,Default,Grace,0,0,0,,we need an ancient ritual \Ncalled a magic-convergence spell.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.68,0:12:00.07,Default,Grace,0,0,0,,First, I'll teach you the \Nfundamentals of ancient rituals.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.38,0:12:04.36,Default,Grace,0,0,0,,Here is the manual \NSaint Philia prepared for us.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.83,0:12:09.74,Default,Grace,0,0,0,,To begin, we should practice mana perception \Nwith a spell called Robe of Light.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.64,0:12:12.95,Default,Emily,0,0,0,,Let's see...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.48,0:12:16.54,Default,Emily,0,0,0,,So it goes like... this?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.98,0:12:18.01,Default,Emily,0,0,0,,Come, light...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.34,0:12:25.38,Default,Grace,0,0,0,,{\i1}She mastered the Robe of Light instantly?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.80,0:12:30.89,Default,Emily,0,0,0,,C-Clear proof of my inborn talent!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.89,0:12:34.64,Default,Emily,0,0,0,,I certainly don't owe it to Philia Adenauer!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.14,0:12:38.18,Main - Italics,Emily,0,0,0,,This...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.29,0:12:42.55,Main - Italics,Emily,0,0,0,,What in the world is this?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.55,0:12:44.10,Main - Italics,Emily,0,0,0,,It's incredible.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.99,0:12:46.80,Default,Emily,0,0,0,,This is too great a gift.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.74,0:12:52.02,Default,Emily,0,0,0,,We'd shame the Mattilas family \Nto remain so deeply in her debt!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.02,0:12:53.59,Default,Emily,0,0,0,,Amanda! Jane!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.59,0:12:56.92,Default,Emily,0,0,0,,Let's learn this magic-convergence \Nspell as quickly as possible!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.92,0:13:00.72,Default,Emily,0,0,0,,We'll show them what \Nthe saints of Bolmern can do!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.72,0:13:02.14,Default,Jane,0,0,0,,Let's do it!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.22,0:13:06.34,Default,Grace,0,0,0,,{\i1}Everything's going to work out!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.83,0:13:09.89,Default,Pierre,0,0,0,,Saint Mia!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.97,0:13:13.06,Default,Pierre,0,0,0,,Prince Julius is making his move.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.26,0:13:18.77,Default,Pierre,0,0,0,,I wasn't expecting Prince Fernand's \Nprovocation to work so quickly.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.77,0:13:24.28,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,This is absurdly rash for the \Nsupposed leader of a kingdom, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.90,0:13:27.44,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}Though that's to our benefit this time.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.01,0:13:28.74,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,What has he done?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.01,0:13:33.33,Default,Pierre,0,0,0,,He's ordered House Adenauer \Nto throw a large party.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.20,0:13:36.92,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,A party?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.18,0:13:40.62,Flashback,George,0,0,0,,Now is when we nobles must band together!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.62,0:13:43.78,Default,Pierre,0,0,0,,And he's invited most of the noble families.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.82,0:13:49.59,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I can't follow that man's logic at all!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.99,0:13:54.10,Default,Nun,0,0,0,,Saint Mia!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.70,0:13:59.38,Default,Nun,0,0,0,,Thank goodness. I was waiting for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.38,0:14:00.19,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.86,0:14:03.68,Default,Nun,0,0,0,,Well, you see...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.68,0:14:05.68,Default,Nun,0,0,0,,A man came in for confession,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.68,0:14:09.16,Default,Nun,0,0,0,,and he insists that you be the one to hear it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.02,0:14:16.06,Main - Italics,Mia,0,0,0,,The son of Marquis Pyrz\N from the second prince faction!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.82,0:14:19.04,Default,Pyrz's Son,0,0,0,,I hope you'll forgive my intrusion.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.63,0:14:24.32,Default,Pyrz's Son,0,0,0,,The truth is... there's something \NI wanted to tell you.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.57,0:14:34.97,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,What an exhausting day...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.55,0:14:37.52,Default,George,0,0,0,,What in the world?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.52,0:14:39.74,Default,George,0,0,0,,Nobody called for you!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.74,0:14:42.49,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}What's all the racket?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.74,0:14:42.49,Main - Top,George,0,0,0,,What's wrong with you? \NWhat are you doing here?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.49,0:14:46.44,Default,George,0,0,0,,You're not welcome here, Hildegarde!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.81,0:14:48.19,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}Auntie?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.22,0:14:52.85,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,It's unbecoming for the head \Nof a household to shout like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.65,0:14:57.70,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,I've come to share information \Nwith Mia, as a fellow saint.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.70,0:15:00.25,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,I'll leave the moment I'm finished.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.35,0:15:04.28,Default,Geroge,0,0,0,,Then do it and get out already!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.28,0:15:06.94,Default,Geroge,0,0,0,,Some saint you are, at your age...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.30,0:15:10.31,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,It's a bit noisy here.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.31,0:15:12.39,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,Care to join me outside?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.67,0:15:14.33,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,O-Of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.52,0:15:23.77,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I haven't seen her in so long...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.36,0:15:27.57,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}She and Big Sister Philia \Nreally do look alike!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.80,0:15:32.32,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}No, knock it off!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.98,0:15:41.18,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,I'm so grateful you've resumed\N your saintly duties, Auntie.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.18,0:15:45.02,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,Thanks to you, we've managed \Nto halt the monsters' advance.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.02,0:15:46.67,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,No need to flatter me.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.20,0:15:50.00,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,My return is but a drop in the ocean.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.64,0:15:54.93,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,This kingdom is on the verge \Nof falling to the monsters.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.97,0:15:57.85,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,A truly deplorable state of affairs.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.58,0:16:03.11,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,My pupil, Philia, could have \Nsolved this entirely on her own...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.77,0:16:04.60,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}That's true.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.24,0:16:08.65,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}We're only slowing them down. \NWe haven't done anything real.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.57,0:16:10.86,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,Well then, Auntie...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.38,0:16:12.92,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,What did you want to discuss?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.11,0:16:16.12,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,Allow me to get right to the point.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.09,0:16:20.12,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,Mia, will you let me adopt you?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.22,0:16:22.09,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.04,0:16:27.17,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,Sooner or later, your parents \Nwill meet their ruin.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.17,0:16:33.50,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,Your revenge is going to condemn them \Nas surely as it does Prince Julius.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.50,0:16:35.84,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}She knows about that?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.56,0:16:39.60,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,I am part of the crown prince faction.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.07,0:16:45.79,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,Prince Julius sold away my precious pupil.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.79,0:16:47.73,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,How could I ever forgive him?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.43,0:16:51.53,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,Pierre told me that you'd joined our side,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.53,0:16:54.03,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,so I've waited for a chance to talk with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.75,0:16:57.74,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,You're sure to struggle \Nafter losing your parents.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.24,0:17:00.49,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,I have also lost my husband,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.88,0:17:04.17,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,but I'm sure I can find a way to support you.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.17,0:17:05.00,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.90,0:17:10.28,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,You barely even know me. \NWhy would you adopt me?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.28,0:17:11.76,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,What does that matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.14,0:17:16.70,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,Your parents already stole {\i1}my{\i0} daughter.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.34,0:17:26.56,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,No...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.72,0:17:29.14,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,You can't mean...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.14,0:17:32.92,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,Would you like to hear an old story?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.36,0:17:40.12,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,My younger brother—\Nyour father, Marquis Adenauer—
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.12,0:17:45.71,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,was jealous of the attention our \Nmother gave me, as a future saint.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.71,0:17:49.33,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,In time, he came to resent and despise me.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.62,0:17:53.35,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,He began to spread malicious lies about me,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.35,0:17:55.34,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,and by the time our mother passed,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.34,0:17:59.14,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,everyone around us had come \Nto believe his lies.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.14,0:18:02.75,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,Though I was a saint, \NI was driven from our home
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.75,0:18:06.41,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,and lost my standing as a \Nmember of House Adenauer.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.41,0:18:12.01,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,My younger brother, then poised \Nto carry on the family line, got married,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.01,0:18:14.73,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,but they failed to bear a child.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.06,0:18:19.74,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,As the head of a family of saints, it was \Nimperative that he produce a daughter.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.32,0:18:25.75,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,And so they set their eyes on Philia, \Nwith whom I was pregnant at the time.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.75,0:18:29.04,Flashback,George,0,0,0,,If it's a girl, I'll use her!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.04,0:18:32.56,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,When he learned she was a girl,\N he stole her from me
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.56,0:18:36.88,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,and spread rumors that my baby was stillborn.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.14,0:18:40.31,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,When I told people Philia was my daughter,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.31,0:18:46.31,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,they thought I'd simply gone mad \Nwith grief from losing my child.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.66,0:18:51.93,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,Soon after, my husband who'd recently\Nfallen ill took a turn for the worse.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.93,0:18:54.45,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,And so I lost him as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.45,0:18:59.82,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,Brokenhearted, I lost \Nthe will to fight altogether.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.39,0:19:04.10,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,In the end, the only \Nthing I could do for her
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.10,0:19:07.91,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,was ensure she was strong enough \Nto stand on her own.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.30,0:19:12.04,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,After all, for letting her go \Nin the first place,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.04,0:19:14.64,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,I am unworthy to call myself a mother.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.64,0:19:17.10,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,I have no intention of telling her.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.10,0:19:20.68,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,But... then why did you tell me?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.22,0:19:22.33,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,Why?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.33,0:19:26.77,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,I'm their real daughter! \NWhy would you tell me that?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.82,0:19:29.68,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,The reason is simple.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.39,0:19:33.77,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,This is my own revenge.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.66,0:19:44.45,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,It worked, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.34,0:19:48.09,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}Because, as awful as they've been,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.09,0:19:50.96,Main - Italics,Mia,0,0,0,,I felt they had to have \N{\i0}some{\i1} goodness in them.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.96,0:19:57.46,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}But now, what little hope I clung \Nto has been completely wiped away.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.72,0:20:03.81,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}Moreover, because those awful people \Neventually had a daughter of their own...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.81,0:20:08.47,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}That means I'm the reason they \Ntreated my sister so awfully!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.47,0:20:10.74,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'm so sorry, Philia!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.74,0:20:15.36,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have no right to call myself your sister!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.34,0:20:20.36,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,If what you say is true,\Nthis makes even less sense.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.77,0:20:23.81,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,Why would you adopt your \Nbeloathed brother's daughter?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.49,0:20:28.87,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,I received a letter from Parnacorta.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.60,0:20:31.79,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,It was from Philia.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.29,0:20:38.04,Default,Hildegarde,0,0,0,,She wrote at great length \Nof how worried she is for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.14,0:20:43.51,Flashback - Italics,Philia,0,0,0,,Please, help the current saint, \NMia, however you can.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.51,0:20:47.47,Flashback - Italics,Philia,0,0,0,,She's very kind, and also very strong.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.77,0:20:50.44,Flashback - Italics,Philia,0,0,0,,She puts all her heart \Ninto anything she tries
Dialogue: 0,0:20:50.44,0:20:52.12,Flashback - Italics,Philia,0,0,0,,and sometimes pushes herself too hard,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.12,0:20:53.89,Flashback - Italics,Philia,0,0,0,,so I'm worried about her.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.24,0:20:56.57,Flashback - Italics,Philia,0,0,0,,Mia is my younger sister.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:56.57,0:20:59.42,Flashback - Italics,Philia,0,0,0,,Unlike me, she's a very good girl.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.47,0:21:02.15,Flashback - Italics,Philia,0,0,0,,I love her very much.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.92,0:21:05.47,Flashback - Italics,Philia,0,0,0,,When my engagement \Nto Prince Julius was decided
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.47,0:21:07.41,Flashback - Italics,Philia,0,0,0,,and I was called back to House Adenauer,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.11,0:21:12.47,Flashback - Italics,Philia,0,0,0,,I felt no connection whatsoever to that place,\Nwhich should have felt like home.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.07,0:21:16.62,Flashback - Italics,Philia,0,0,0,,But Mia welcomed me so warmly.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.09,0:21:18.67,Flashback,Mia,0,0,0,,Welcome home!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.67,0:21:24.26,Flashback - Italics,Philia,0,0,0,,I believe it only became my home \Nbecause she was there.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.11,0:21:29.55,Flashback - Italics,Philia,0,0,0,,I didn't realize I felt that way at the time.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.55,0:21:33.68,Flashback - Italics,Philia,0,0,0,,But having learned in Parnacorta \Nto look back on my life with clarity,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.68,0:21:35.27,Flashback - Italics,Philia,0,0,0,,I think I can see now...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.91,0:21:40.70,Flashback - Italics,Philia,0,0,0,,that Mia's kindness has saved me.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.89,0:21:46.28,Flashback - Italics,Philia,0,0,0,,I believe Girtonia needs the light she shines.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:47.36,0:21:49.53,Flashback - Italics,Philia,0,0,0,,So I ask of you, my mentor...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.56,0:21:53.91,Flashback - Italics,Philia,0,0,0,,Please be there for Mia.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:26.95,0:23:32.34,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}The Too-Perfect Saint Tossed Aside by \NMy Fiancé and Sold to Another Kingdom{\i0}.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:33.44,0:23:35.05,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Next time, episode 9:
